<%# app/views/election/receipt_spec/show.html.erb
    Canonical receipt payload spec — versioned at /spec/receipt-v1.
    Third-party verifiers (CEP tablets, journalists, NGOs) consume this
    page to build interoperable Ed25519 verification tooling. %>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="<%= I18n.locale %>">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>BonVote Receipt v1 — Verification Spec</title>
  <meta name="description" content="Canonical signing-payload specification for BonVote voter receipts.">
  <%= render "election/shared/bonvote_theme", sparkle_count: 4 %>
  <style>
    .spec-shell { max-width: 880px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1rem; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.85); }
    .spec-shell h1 { color: #fff; font-weight: 800; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
    .spec-shell h2 { color: var(--ht-gold, #EDB95E); font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.15rem; margin-top: 2rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em; }
    .spec-shell h3 { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.95); font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-top: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
    .spec-shell p  { font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.65; color: #B8C2D1; }
    .spec-shell code, .spec-shell pre {
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      color: rgba(255,255,255,0.92);
    }
    .spec-shell pre {
      background: rgba(0,0,0,0.35);
      border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);
      border-radius: 0.5rem;
      padding: 1rem;
      overflow-x: auto;
      line-height: 1.55;
    }
    .spec-shell code {
      background: rgba(0,0,0,0.35);
      padding: 0.1rem 0.35rem;
      border-radius: 0.25rem;
    }
    .spec-shell pre code { background: transparent; padding: 0; }
    .spec-shell table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.82rem; margin: 0.75rem 0 1rem; }
    .spec-shell th, .spec-shell td { padding: 0.55rem 0.75rem; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
    .spec-shell th { color: var(--ht-gold, #EDB95E); font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 0.7rem; letter-spacing: 0.05em; }
    .spec-shell ul { padding-left: 1.25rem; }
    .spec-shell li { margin-bottom: 0.35rem; font-size: 0.9rem; color: #B8C2D1; }
    .spec-shell a { color: var(--ht-gold, #EDB95E); text-decoration: none; }
    .spec-shell a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
    .spec-meta { font-size: 0.78rem; color: #64748B; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
    .spec-warn {
      background: rgba(220,53,69,0.08);
      border-left: 3px solid #DC3545;
      padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
      border-radius: 0.4rem;
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      color: rgba(255,255,255,0.85);
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="spec-shell">
    <h1>BonVote Receipt — Verification Spec v1</h1>
    <div class="spec-meta">
      Version <code>v1</code> &middot; Algorithm <code>Ed25519</code> &middot;
      Stable contract &middot; <a href="<%= election_verify_receipt_path %>">Open verifier</a>
    </div>

    <p>
      A BonVote voter receipt carries a compact JSON payload and an Ed25519
      signature produced by BonID. Anyone — citizen, observer, journalist —
      can reconstruct the canonical signing input from the payload alone
      and verify the signature against the election's public key. This
      page is the canonical description of that procedure.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Payload shape</h2>
    <p>The QR code on a receipt encodes a verify URL of the form:</p>
    <pre><code>https://bonid.ht/election/verify-receipt?d=&lt;base64url(payload_json)&gt;</code></pre>
    <p>where <code>payload_json</code> is the UTF-8 JSON object below.</p>

    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>v</code></td>   <td>integer</td><td>Payload version (always <code>1</code> for this spec).</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>ref</code></td> <td>string</td> <td>Voter reference. Format <code>BVT-YYYY-XXXX-YYYY</code> (BonID-issued, not a CEP credential).</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>bon</code></td> <td>string</td> <td>Truncated BonID (first 12 chars) — enough to disambiguate without leaking the full identifier.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>e</code></td>   <td>integer</td><td>BonVote election ID. Used to look up the right public key.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>bv</code></td>  <td>integer</td><td>Assigned Biwo Vòt number (optional — absent before assignment).</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>c</code></td>   <td>string</td> <td>Polling-center display name (optional).</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>kid</code></td> <td>string</td> <td>Key identifier. Format <code>bonvote-election-&lt;id&gt;-&lt;YYYY-MM&gt;</code>. Tells the verifier which key (current or archived) to use.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>s</code></td>   <td>string</td> <td>Base64url Ed25519 signature (no padding) over the canonical JSON of the payload <strong>excluding the <code>s</code> field itself</strong>.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>2. Canonical signing payload</h2>
    <p>
      To verify, strip the <code>s</code> field and serialize the remaining
      object using these rules:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Object keys sorted lexicographically (string compare).</li>
      <li>No whitespace (no spaces, no newlines).</li>
      <li>UTF-8 encoding.</li>
      <li>Standard JSON value escaping (the same encoding any JSON library produces).</li>
      <li>Arrays preserve insertion order; nested objects sorted recursively.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>This is the byte string that was signed.</p>

    <h3>Example</h3>
    <pre><code>{
  "v":   1,
  "ref": "BVT-2026-3SYB-RMKP",
  "bon": "DL-1988-M-OU",
  "e":   3,
  "bv":  1,
  "c":   "Lekòl Nasyonal Kenscoff",
  "kid": "bonvote-election-3-2026-04",
  "s":   "uySu8y90PHgB8b9NiN_WgluXLKBMmhzZ-PFw8bE5..."
}</code></pre>

    <p>Canonical signing input (after stripping <code>s</code>, sorting, no whitespace):</p>
    <pre><code>{"bon":"DL-1988-M-OU","bv":1,"c":"Lekòl Nasyonal Kenscoff","e":3,"kid":"bonvote-election-3-2026-04","ref":"BVT-2026-3SYB-RMKP","v":1}</code></pre>

    <h2>3. Public key lookup</h2>
    <p>Fetch the election's key bundle from:</p>
    <pre><code>GET /api/v1/elections/&lt;e&gt;/bonvote_public_key</code></pre>
    <p>The response includes the current key plus every archived key:</p>
    <pre><code>{
  "algorithm": "Ed25519",
  "encoding":  "base64",
  "issuer":    "bonvote.ht",
  "election":  { "id": 3, "title": "...", "round": 1, "status": "open" },
  "current":   { "key_id": "bonvote-election-3-2026-04", "public_key_b64": "...", "key_fingerprint": "..." },
  "archived":  [ { "key_id": "...", "public_key_b64": "...", "key_fingerprint": "..." } ]
}</code></pre>

    <p>
      Match the receipt's <code>kid</code> against <code>current.key_id</code>
      first, then against each entry in <code>archived</code>. If no match
      is found the receipt cannot be verified — a <code>kid</code>-less
      receipt (legacy) falls back to the current key.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Signature verification</h2>
    <p>
      Decode <code>s</code> with base64url (RFC 4648 §5, no padding). Decode
      <code>public_key_b64</code> with standard base64. Run Ed25519 verify
      per <a href="https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8032">RFC 8032</a>:
    </p>
    <pre><code>ed25519_verify(public_key, canonical_signing_input, signature) -> true | false</code></pre>

    <p>A returned <code>true</code> means BonID issued this receipt under the named key. <code>false</code> means the receipt was tampered, the signature is forged, or the wrong key was tried.</p>

    <h2>5. Reference verifier</h2>
    <p>
      The hosted verifier at <a href="<%= election_verify_receipt_path %>"><%= election_verify_receipt_path %></a>
      implements exactly this procedure. Source is in
      <code>app/services/election/bonvote_signing_service.rb</code> and
      <code>app/controllers/election/verify_receipt_controller.rb</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Key rotation</h2>
    <p>
      When BonID rotates a signing key, the old <code>{key_id, public_key_b64}</code>
      pair is appended to the election's archived key list. Receipts signed
      under the old key continue to verify forever — the <code>kid</code>
      on the receipt picks the correct historical key.
    </p>

    <div class="spec-warn">
      <strong>Note.</strong> The signature attests that BonID issued this
      receipt according to BonVote's protocol — not that the citizen voted,
      not that CEP recognized the registration, not that the BV assignment
      is final. Authority over voter rolls remains with CEP per the
      December 1, 2025 decree.
    </div>

    <h2>7. Spec versioning</h2>
    <p>
      This URL — <code>/spec/receipt-v1</code> — is permanent. A payload
      format change becomes <code>/spec/receipt-v2</code>; v1 stays
      canonically described here for any historical receipt issued under
      <code>"v": 1</code>.
    </p>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
